<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41394" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίτον-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on the stretch, strained,
				intense,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				10.17
			</span></i> ; of sound, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VS</u>
				1.25.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίτονος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμάς</span>), ὁ,
				<i>a rope for stretching</i> or <i>tightening, back-stay</i>
			of a mast (opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρότονος</span>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ αὐτῷ [ἱστῷ] ἐπίτονος βέβλητο,
					βοὸς ῥινοῖο τετευχώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.423
				</span></i>
			 (a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στίχος ἀκέφαλος</span>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίτονοι, οἱ,</span> the <i>great sinews of the shoulder and arm,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				84e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				515b9
			</span></i> (sg.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεύρων ἐπίτονοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					945c
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
